  "updateinfo_id": "ALSA-2026:89082",
  "description": "The kernel-rt packages provide the Real Time Linux Kernel, which enables fine-tuning for systems with extremely high determinism requirements.  \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * kernel: tcp: restrict SO_ATTACH_FILTER to priv users (CVE-2026-53236)\n  * kernel: fuse: re-lock request before replacing page cache folio (CVE-2026-53388)\n  * kernel: writeback: fix race between cgroup_writeback_umount() and inode_switch_wbs() (CVE-2026-64378)\n  * kernel: net: gro: fix double aggregation of flush-marked skbs (CVE-2026-68136)\n  * kernel: net/packet: avoid fanout hook re-registration after unregister (CVE-2026-68338)\n  * kernel: net/iucv: fix use-after-free of a severed iucv_path (CVE-2026-68140)\n  * kernel: net/sched: serialize qdisc_rtab_list against concurrent get/put (CVE-2026-68138)\n  * kernel: ipvs: reload ip header after head reallocation (CVE-2026-68476)\n  * kernel: selinux: avoid sk_socket dereference in selinux_sctp_bind_connect() (CVE-2026-72242)\n  * kernel: mptcp: options: reset DSS fields in case of unexpected size (CVE-2026-80586)\n  * kernel: usb: usbfs: fix use-after-free of usb_device in usbdev_release() (CVE-2026-80824)\n  * kernel: smb: client: clear setuid/setgid bit on write with cifsacl/modefromsid/posix extensions (CVE-2026-89638)\n  * kernel: net/iucv: filter frames in afiucv_hs_rcv() by ingress device (CVE-2026-81003)\n  * kernel: ipv4: validate checksum_start before completing checksum (CVE-2026-99999)\n\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):  \n\n  * Backport 6785011f8b16 (\"ipv4: validate checksum_start before completing checksum\") [almalinux-8.10.z] (JIRA:AlmaLinux-280584)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n",
  "fromstr": "packager@almalinux.org",
  "issued_date": {
    "$date": 1792800000000
  },
